  "project": {
    "name": {
      "en": "Accordion fan",
      "es": "Abanico plegable",
      "fr": "Éventail plissé",
      "pt": "Leque plissado"
    },
    "slug": "accordion-fan",
    "version": "0.1.0",
    "engine": "pliego",
    "description": {
      "en": "Two fans on one geometry, the radial pleat: a hand fan whose pleats gather at the base, and the paper leaf of a ribbed folding fan with its card ribs glued on and riveted together. Every crease runs towards one point off the paper, so the pleats close and open rigidly, exact at every step.",
      "es": "Dos abanicos sobre una misma geometría, el plisado radial: un abanico de mano cuyos pliegues se recogen en la base y el país de papel de un abanico de varillas, con sus varillas de cartulina pegadas y remachadas entre sí. Todos los pliegues apuntan a un punto fuera del papel, así que el plisado se cierra y se abre de forma rígida, exacto en cada paso.",
      "fr": "Deux éventails sur une même géométrie, le plissé radial : un éventail à main dont les plis se resserrent à la base, et la feuille de papier d'un éventail à brins, avec ses brins de carton collés et rivetés ensemble. Chaque pli pointe vers un point hors du papier, si bien que le plissé se ferme et s'ouvre de façon rigide, exact à chaque étape.",
      "pt": "Dois leques sobre uma mesma geometria, o plissado radial: um leque de mão cujas pregas se recolhem na base e a folha de papel de um leque de varetas, com as varetas de cartolina coladas e rebitadas entre si. Todas as dobras apontam para um ponto fora do papel, por isso o plissado fecha e abre de forma rígida, exato em cada passo."
    },
    "thumbnail": "/projects/accordion-fan.svg",
    "difficulty": "beginner",
    "tags": [
      "fan",
      "pleat",
      "rigid-origami",
      "multi-sheet",
      "hyperobject",
      "commons"
    ],
    "attribution": {
      "author": "Innovaciones MADFAM",
      "license": "CERN-OHL-W-2.0",
      "lineage": [
        {
          "source": "Original MADFAM geometry generated by this cartridge (radial pleat in closed form); the object types are traditional — the pleated paper hand fan and the ribbed folding fan, generally traced to Japan (sensu, ōgi) — and no maker's fan design is copied",
          "license": "original"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
